# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Without this, files committed from Windows are stored with CRLF and every
# clone gets CRLF — including on Linux. That breaks two things badly:
#
#   * a shell script whose shebang reads `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` fails with
#     "bad interpreter: No such file or directory", which is a confusing way
#     to learn about line endings
#   * shellcheck reports SC1017 on every line and the CI job fails
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores everything with LF and checks it out with LF, on
# every platform. The files here are all destined for a Linux machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the ones that are executed rather than read.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer   text eol=lf
